From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 02:35:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: start the MAC work of running radios only
 after a reset

mt7996_reconfig_complete() queues the MAC work of every radio, also of
a radio without interface.  Nothing cancels it there, since
mt7996_stop_phy() only stops running radios, and the work queues itself
again forever.  When the driver is removed, its timer can then fire
after the workqueue of the hardware is gone and crash the kernel.

Queue the MAC work of running radios only, as mt7996_run() does.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 mt7996/main.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -2615,8 +2615,9 @@ mt7996_reconfig_complete(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 
 	ieee80211_wake_queues(hw);
 	mt7996_for_each_phy(dev, phy)
-		ieee80211_queue_delayed_work(hw, &phy->mt76->mac_work,
-					     MT7996_WATCHDOG_TIME);
+		if (test_bit(MT76_STATE_RUNNING, &phy->mt76->state))
+			ieee80211_queue_delayed_work(hw, &phy->mt76->mac_work,
+						     MT7996_WATCHDOG_TIME);
 }
 
 static int
